# Au - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, the reference parameters
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * Au.ugur Au
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 does not vanish at rcut2, it stops at -0.403 meV (0.0158 of k_B T at 296 K).  USE for static properties and for lattice dynamics: measured against neutron dispersion the hard sets average 9.5 % over the 29 elements that have one, against 12.6 % for the switched sets, and are closer in 24 of them.  DO NOT use for molecular dynamics: copper, whose step is 8.4 meV, drifts 350 meV/atom/ns in NVE and climbs from 296 K to over 1100 K in 200 ps
# MD: structure screened - holds its shape at 600 K (307 K, as equipartition requires).  This tested the SHAPE, not energy conservation; for that see the truncation line above.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Au at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Au Au Au 8.0674980772727896 0.83743383388585846 0.70359232925504345 2.7297843606995218 1.6453501069431855 -4.5348712858259645 1.1864389656682701 10.60332 4.3255843125524667 -1 0 0
